Change to: properties as ["kind", "name"].

# Notes
- Added configuration endpoint for members
- Added new ConfigurationPresentationFactory, that is responsible for creating the configuration models
- Added new `IReservedNamesService` that will return all the reserved names for a given model (Member, Media, Content)
- Added 3 new property settings, so that users (or package devs) can define their own reserved names.

# How to test
- Using the 3 configuration endpoint, assert that you get the correct list of reserved names
- Try configuring the property settings & add some reserved names yourself, assert these also get returned via the endpoints
- You can use this code to configure the property settings:

```
public class TestComposer : IComposer
{
    public void Compose(IUmbracoBuilder builder) =>
        builder.Services.Configure<ContentPropertySettings>(
            x =>
            {
                x.AddReservedFieldName("myReservedFieldName");
                x.AddReservedFieldName("anotherOne");
            });
}

```

usage:
```
// stack usages
const s3 = new S3Stack([
		// public bucket with ability to sync files from a folder
		{
			bucketName: 'config',
			removalPolicy: 'destroy', // Delete the bucket when the stack is deleted
			autoDeleteObjects: true, // Delete all objects when the bucket is deleted
			source: './data', // Sync data from this folder on deploy
			publicReadAccess: false, // Make the bucket public
		},
		// private bucket to upload files from application
		{
			bucketName: 'upload',
			removalPolicy: 'destroy', // Delete the bucket when the stack is deleted
			autoDeleteObjects: true, // Delete all objects when the bucket is deleted
		},
		// private bucket with notification to lambda function
		{
			bucketName: 'import-lambda',
			removalPolicy: 'destroy', // Delete the bucket when the stack is deleted
			autoDeleteObjects: true, // Delete all objects when the bucket is deleted
			triggers: [
				{
					events: [ EventType.OBJECT_CREATED ],
					destination: 'lambda',
					handler: './src/functions/import.ts',
				}
			],
		},
		// private bucket with notification to a queue
		{
			bucketName: 'import-queue',
			removalPolicy: 'destroy', // Delete the bucket when the stack is deleted
			autoDeleteObjects: true, // Delete all objects when the bucket is deleted
			triggers: [
				{
					events: [ EventType.OBJECT_REMOVED_DELETE ],
					destination: 'queue',
					queueName: 'import'
				},
			],
		}
	],
);


// in application controller
// add lambda permission to write to bucket
@Controller('auth', { 
	buckets: [
		{ name: 'sandbox-app-bucket' }
	]
})

```
